{% doc %}
  How many of today's Yoink have actually been taken.

  THIS USED TO BE A "% CLAIMED" BAR AND AN "ONLY N LEFT" LINE. Both rested on
  `units_allocated` being a limit we would honour. It never was — nothing in the
  app or the theme caps sales at the allocation — and the decision is that
  nothing should: if a supplier has stock, we want to sell it. That makes "Only
  12 left" false at the moment it is printed, on a product where the supplier
  holds fourteen thousand. It is the exact shape of manufactured scarcity that
  `decisions.md` rules out, arrived at by accident rather than intent.

  So the scarcity claim goes and the count stays. Two kinds of urgency remain,
  and both are real:

    TIME — the countdown, which targets an absolute timestamp.
    MOMENTUM — this, which counts units that genuinely sold.

  Momentum cannot become a lie however much we sell, which is exactly why it
  survives a decision to sell everything available. A percentage cannot: it
  needs a denominator, and the only denominator on offer is a number we have
  decided not to enforce.

  HOW THE COUNT IS DERIVED. The supplier holds the inventory and it is enormous
  relative to the deal, so inventory is snapshotted when the deal opens and the
  delta is what sold:

      sold = starting_inventory − inventory on hand now

  With no snapshot it falls back to the allocation, which is true when we hold
  the stock ourselves. A supplier restocking mid-deal makes the delta understate
  what sold; it cannot overstate it, so the number errs low — the safe direction
  for a figure whose whole job is to be believed.

  Renders NOTHING when it cannot be truthful or would undersell:
    * the product does not track inventory in Shopify
    * nothing has sold yet
    * fewer than `min_sold` have sold — "3 yoinked today" argues against the
      deal exactly as "3% claimed" did. Selective disclosure of a real number,
      never an adjusted one.

  @param {object} product - The deal product.
  @param {number} units_allocated - Units committed. Only a fallback basis now.
  @param {number} [starting_inventory] - Inventory on hand when the deal opened.
  @param {number} [min_sold] - Hide below this count. 0 shows any non-zero count.
  @param {string} [label] - Wording. `[count]` is replaced with the number.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign allocated = units_allocated | plus: 0
  assign snapshot = starting_inventory | plus: 0
  assign tracked = false
  assign remaining = 0

  comment
    Sum across variants. A variant with inventory_management unset is untracked,
    and Shopify reports inventory_quantity 0 for those — counting it would read
    as sold and inflate the number.
  endcomment
  for variant in product.variants
    if variant.inventory_management == 'shopify'
      assign tracked = true
      if variant.inventory_quantity > 0
        assign remaining = remaining | plus: variant.inventory_quantity
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  if snapshot > 0
    assign sold = snapshot | minus: remaining
  else
    assign sold = allocated | minus: remaining
  endif

  comment
    Negative means stock went UP since the snapshot — a supplier restock, or a
    stale allocation. Report nothing sold rather than a negative count.
  endcomment
  if sold < 0
    assign sold = 0
  endif

  assign floor_count = min_sold | plus: 0

  assign show = false
  if tracked and sold > 0 and sold >= floor_count
    assign show = true
  endif
-%}

{{ "aj-deal.css" | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- if show -%}
  {%- assign wording = label | default: '[count] yoinked today' -%}
  <p class="aj-claimed__count">
    <strong>{{ wording | replace: '[count]', sold }}</strong>
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
